{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context\nRP-01 proposes replacing Rebar’s bespoke structured-output orchestration with authoritative Pydantic AI seams. The replacement is not behavior-preserving by default: historical bugs encode hard-won behavior around deterministic repair and extraction, refusal/truncation handling, retry and tool/request limits, per-operation output budgets, provider fallback, usage accounting, telemetry, and failure taxonomy. Before RP-01 can be approved or ticketized, reconstruct the behavioral contract from both ticket history and the existing test suite and exercise the worktree virtualenv’s resolved Pydantic AI distribution. A behavior may be preserved or intentionally changed, but no observed delta may be accidental or left to the implementer.\n\nThe checkout-local probe path is `.joe-janitor/rp01-pydantic-native-probe.py`. The entire `.joe-janitor/` archive is intentionally excluded from repository snapshots, so an attested-source reviewer cannot see this path; use the existing local file when present and create it at that exact path if absent. The worktree virtualenv resolves `pydantic-ai-slim` to exactly 1.107.2, verified with `python -c \"import importlib.metadata; print(importlib.metadata.version('pydantic-ai-slim'))\"`; the probe must print and record that resolved version rather than infer it from the repository’s `>=1.107,<2` range.\n\n## Plan\n- Deduplicate ticket-derived scenarios with behavioral cases from the structured runner, failure-matrix, budget, timeout, and agent-call seam test suites.\n- Record each scenario’s current observable behavior and its authoritative ticket/test evidence.\n- Continue or create the checkout-local `.joe-janitor/rp01-pydantic-native-probe.py` to exercise Pydantic AI 1.107.2 native output, prompted output, output retry, usage limits, FallbackModel predicates, provider errors, truncation/refusal, telemetry, and artifact-capture feasibility without live model calls.\n- Classify each scenario as preserve, intentionally change, or requiring an explicit maintainer decision; do not infer an invariant from the current implementation alone.\n- Record the resulting evidence and experiment outputs in the local `.joe-janitor/` recovery archive and summarize the decision matrix on this ticket.\n\n## Verification\nThis is an investigation task. The behavior-crossing tier is an in-process integration probe using the real Pydantic AI 1.107.2 Agent/FunctionModel/output/limits/hooks seams while mocking only provider transport. The oracle is the exact call count, request mode, accepted semantic output, exception class, usage/accounting fields, and captured telemetry for each predeclared scenario. Existing unit tests provide the current-Rebar side of the comparison. Run the probe with `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" python .joe-janitor/rp01-pydantic-native-probe.py`; it must report the resolved `pydantic-ai-slim` version as 1.107.2 before its scenario results.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] The matrix maps every material ticket-derived scenario to exact ticket aliases.\n- [x] The matrix maps every material test-derived scenario to exact test nodes or source locations.\n- [x] The matrix states current Rebar behavior for every scenario.\n- [x] The matrix states observed Pydantic AI 1.107.2 behavior for every exercised scenario.\n- [x] Every outcome difference is labeled preserve, intentionally change, or explicit decision required; no difference is silently inherited from either implementation.\n- [x] The offline probe executes the real Pydantic AI output/retry/fallback/limits/hook seams and records exact observable oracles without a live model call.\n- [x] The RP-01 research note is stored under `.joe-janitor/` beside the recovered janitor report.\n- [x] The Pydantic probe is stored at `.joe-janitor/rp01-pydantic-native-probe.py`.\n- [x] [operator-attested] A ticket comment records the artifact paths, probe command and result, scenario coverage totals, and the next unresolved behavior decision.\n  provenance: environment=local-checkout-b0aac2314; principal=joeoakhart@navapbc.com; privilege_posture=production-equivalent; instrument=live-call — Read back the ticket comment and compare each recorded artifact path, command result, coverage total, and decision against the local research note."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786908094725955001,"uuid":"e1b4798f-ac6b-4c3c-a00d-89959662fa4c"}